  /* Free tabs (edit mode) — the canonical Schema recipe: .sch-tabbar / .sch-gtabs live
     in global.css, so nothing about the tabs themselves is styled here.
     On /schema the tab row owns the full width, so ITS border is the divider. Here the
     row shares the strip with Cancel / Save, so borrowing that border stopped the rule
     dead under the buttons. The BAR keeps the divider instead — it spans the whole
     container — and the tab row's own border is switched off so the two don't stack into
     a doubled hairline. Tabs still sit flush on it: align-items: flex-end + no bottom
     padding on the bar. */
  .bar:has(.sch-tabbar) { align-items: flex-end; padding-bottom: 0; }
